    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21566" root="شبح" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشْبُوحٌ</span></b>  <i>Wide between the shoulders.</i> (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشْبُوحُ الذِّرَاعَيْنِ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الذِّرَاعَيْنِ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَبْحُ</span></b>  A man
<i>broad in the fore arms:</i> (S, K:) or <i>long therein:</i>
but AAF and Ibn-El-Jowzee prefer the former
explanation. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشْبُوحٌ بِأَمْر ٍ</span> <i>Attached,</i> or
<i>addicted, to an affair;</i> or <i>fond of it.</i> (O.)

